n (1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000). The second line contains c1 and n1 , and the third line contains c2 and n2 .
Here, c1 , c2 , n1 and n2 are all positive integers having values smaller than 2,000,000,000.
   A test case containing a zero for n in the first line terminates the input.', 'For each test case in the input print a line containing the minimum cost solution (two nonnegative
integers m1 and m2 , where mi = number of T ypei boxes required) if one exists, print ‘failed’ otherwise.
    If a solution exists, you may assume that it is unique.', '(1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000)', '[{"input":"The input file may contain multiple test cases. Each test case begins with a line containing the integer\nn (1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000). The second line contains c1 and n1 , and the third line contains c2 and n2 .\nHere, c1 , c2 , n1 and n2 are all positive integers having values smaller than 2,000,000,000.\n   A test case containing a zero for n in the first line terminates the input.","output":"For each test case in the input print a line containing the minimum cost solution (two nonnegative\nintegers m1 and m2 , where mi = number of T ypei boxes required) if one exists, print ‘failed’ otherwise.\n    If a solution exists, you may assume that it is unique."}]'::jsonb, 'O(N log N)');
