for 1 ≤ i ≤ N , H1 ̸= HN and Hi ̸= Hi+1 for 1 ≤ i < N ). Notice that H1 follows HN when the loop is
played.
    The end of the input is indicated by a line that contains only one zero.

Universidad de Valladolid OJ: 11496 – Musical Loop                                                   2/2', 'For each test case in the input your program must print a single line, containing one integer, the number
of peaks that exist in the musical loop.', '(2 ≤ N ≤ 104 ) (−104 ≤ Hi ≤ 104
for 1 ≤ i ≤ N , H1 ̸= HN and Hi ̸= Hi+1 for 1 ≤ i < N )', '[{"input":"The input contains several test cases. The first line of a test case contains one integer N , representing the\nnumber of samples in the musical loop composed by Fernanda (2 ≤ N ≤ 104 ). The second line contains\nN integers Hi , separated by spaces, representing the sequence of magnitudes sampled (−104 ≤ Hi ≤ 104\nfor 1 ≤ i ≤ N , H1 ̸= HN and Hi ̸= Hi+1 for 1 ≤ i < N ). Notice that H1 follows HN when the loop is\nplayed.\n    The end of the input is indicated by a line that contains only one zero.\n\nUniversidad de Valladolid OJ: 11496 – Musical Loop                                                   2/2","output":"For each test case in the input your program must print a single line, containing one integer, the number\nof peaks that exist in the musical loop."}]'::jsonb, 'O(N log N)');
